  "_comment": "Canonical vocabulary — the single source of concept/skill IDs + the 9 axes. Hand-curated CANON (committed, NOT gitignored; contains no personal study data). capture.mjs READS this to normalize a rep's concept (case-fold + alias lookup) and to flag unregistered:true; capture NEVER writes it (single-writer preserved). track:\"concept\" IDs = AI concepts (9-axis, decay-prone); track:\"skill\" IDs = Python + hands-on/course work (fluency, NO axis). Grows over time; adding an entry retro-registers matching reps on next load.",
  "_track_rule": "capture.mjs accepts EXACTLY two tracks: concept and skill. sprint.json also carries course/build/domain/career — those are CURRICULUM labels, not rep tracks. Mapping of record, verbatim from .claude/skills/learn/SKILL.md §track routing: course -> track:\"skill\" (surface \"colab\", axis null), subject registered under \"skills\" below · build -> track:\"skill\" too (\"there is no build rep track\") — its reps land on the Python/API skills the build exercises (fastapi, pydantic, parsers, api_error_handling), not on task nouns like \"scaffold\" or \"vercel deploy\" · domain (TDS/TCS/DTAA) -> track:\"concept\", registered below, because it produces genuine recall reps · career -> no reps. Registered 30 Jul 2026 from sprint.json after an audit found only 8 of ~115 sprint strings resolved — every unregistered concept silently coined a phantom topic that grew its own FSRS cards and nemesis entries. (Corrected same day: the first version wrongly claimed build/domain produce no reps.)",
  "_unregistered_note": "1-09 'Recall + Bolo locks' is deliberately NOT a concept: it is the method (blank-recall, spoken explain, capsule lock), not a body of knowledge with 9 axes.",
